R"VG(
# futuristic.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the machine's log (drives and crystals): a day of the habitat's keeping in the log's
# register (`@news public log`), its lines composed of parts that are the people's own: the systems it keeps (by the ruins' plan, its
# links, its light, its land: a terraced people's log keeps the terraces), the residents' requests and the answers, what they did
# (their feasts, their crafts, their herds kept for the old times' sake), the counts, the weather outside, the decline. Each people
# keeps its own share of every part (`fut.` pools, futuristic5.vg), so two peoples' machines never log the same day.

@root ar.life.* memorial.*

# ---- the machine's log ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.mlog (words=21..160)
  {ml.head}\n{log.t1} {ml.line}\n{log.t2} {@news public log}\n{log.t3} {ml.line}\n{log.t4} {ml.line}\n{log.t5} {ml.line}
  {ml.head}\n{log.t1} {@news public log}\n{log.t2} {ml.line}\n{log.t4} {ml.line}\n{log.t5} {ml.line}
  {ml.head}\n{log.t1} {ml.line}\n{log.t2} {ml.line}\n{log.t3} {@news public log}\n{log.t5} {ml.line}
  {ml.head}\n{log.t2} {ml.line}\n{log.t3} {ml.line}\n{log.t4} {ml.line}\n{log.t5} {@news public log}

ml.head (formula people=3)
  (has:mind) Log of {mind}, node at {$home}. Cycle {#year:digits}.
  Systems log, {$home}. Cycle {#year:digits}.
  {$home}, the keeping log, cycle {#year:digits}, {season.now}.
  The house log of {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}.
  (has:$home.quarter) Log, {$home}, {$home.quarter}. Cycle {#year:digits}.
  (has:day) The {~log} of {$home}: cycle {#year:digits}, the {#day:ord} day.
  {$home} keeping record. Cycle {#year:digits}. {season.now}.
  Day log of the habitat at {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}.
  Watch log, {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}, {season.now}.

ml.line
  (3 once) {fut.maint}
  (2 once) {fut.maint}
  (2 once) {fut.ask}
  (1.5 once) {fut.obs}
  (1 once) {fut.count}
  (1 once) {fut.outside}
  (1 once) {fut.pens}
  (0.8 once) {fut.rite}
  (1.5 once stage>=1) {fut.decline}

# a system kept: what was done to it, and how it went
fut.maint
  (3) {fut.did} {fut.sys}. {fut.result}
  (2) {fut.sys}: {fut.did.short}. {fut.result}
  (1) {fut.did} {fut.sys}, {fut.cause}. {fut.result}
  (1) {fut.did} {fut.sys} {fut.when.past}. {fut.result}
  (1) {fut.sys} {fut.state}. {fut.did.short}. {fut.result}

fut.did (share=0.6)
  Maintenance completed on
  Inspection of
  A fault cleared in
  Power rerouted to
  A leak sealed in
  Filters changed in
  A noise traced in
  A sensor replaced in
  Stores counted in
  Repainting of
  A draught stopped in
  A crack mended in
  Routine cleaning of
  The night schedule changed for
  The alarms tested in
  The lighting adjusted in
  The old wiring traced in
  The doors serviced in
  Pressure checked in
  A spill cleaned up in
  A drill held in
  The heat raised in
  Dust cleared from
  The {~bolts} replaced in
fut.did.short
  cleaned
  inspected
  repaired
  tested
  repainted
  sealed
  rewired
  counted
  serviced
  aired
  reset
  checked twice

fut.cause
  at the residents' request
  before {festival}
  after {weather.now}
  because the children found it first
  for the {nth} time this cycle
  on the old schedule, which nobody remembers making
  a cycle late
  ahead of {season.next}
  while {fut.res.lc} were at {feast.custom}

fut.state
  ran warm overnight
  made a sound like {fut.sound}
  stopped for {#n|minute}
  was found open
  smelled of {fut.smell}
  dripped onto the {fut.floor}
  flickered {fut.when.past}
  was reported cold by {#n|resident}

fut.result (share=0.75)
  No faults.
  Within limits.
  One part replaced.
  Logged for review.
  Nothing wrong after all.
  The {fut.block} were not disturbed, which is the aim.
  The {fut.block} were disturbed, and said so, at length.
  Nobody in the {fut.block} noticed, which is the aim.
  The fault was {fut.culprit}. Removed.
  Done twice; the first time the {craft} workshop said it was not right.
  {#n|resident} from the {fut.block} watched and offered advice.
  Three hours, most of them waiting for a part from the {craft} workshop.
  The part was older than the {tree} on the slopes.
  It will need doing again before the {bird} come back.
  Finished {fut.when.past}.
  The old way worked better, the {craft} workshop says. Noted.
  The repair is not pretty. It holds, like the old {walls.of}.
  Cost: {#n:words} hours, one argument and a pot of {drink}.
  A child helped. The child's work, a row of {motif.over}, has been left in place.
  The {~guild} were thanked with {food}.
  Recorded in the {~book} as well as here.
  Another layer of paint on the old ones; {motif.over} still show through.
  The {craft} workshop was consulted, at length.
  The {herd} were moved out first and back in after, complaining.
  Done to the sound of {instrument} from the {fut.common}.
  The old ones said it was done better before the {fut.green} were planted. Possibly.
  Paid for with {food} for the workers, as the custom is.
  A {colour.holy} mark painted on it, to show it is done.

fut.culprit
  a {beast} in the ducts
  a nest of {bird}
  a piece from {fut.game} in the vent
  a {vessel.one.n} wedged in the valve
  dust from {land}
  frost on the intake
  a seal older than the habitat
  a wrong setting, made by me

fut.sound
  {bird}
  a {beast} in the walls
  rain on {roofs}
  someone humming
  {instrument} being tuned
  distant applause

fut.smell
  {fuel}
  burnt {food}
  {drink}
  wet stone
  the gardens after rain
  hot metal

# a resident's wish, and the answer
fut.ask
  (3) {fut.asker} asked {fut.wish}. {fut.answer}
  (1) Request from {fut.asker.lc}: {fut.wish.n}. {fut.answer}
  (1) {fut.asker} asked {fut.wish} again. {fut.answer}
  (1) {fut.asker} came to the panel and asked {fut.wish}. {fut.answer}

fut.asker (people=10)
  A child of {n}
  The oldest resident of {$home}
  A gardener from the {fut.green}
  A visitor from {city2}
  The master of the {craft} workshop
  Two sisters from the {fut.block}
  A man who keeps the {herd} in the heritage pens
  (has:$home.quarter) A woman from {$home.quarter}
  A boy who wants to be a {fut.dream}
  The watch at the {fut.gate}
  A new mother in the {fut.block}
  The {~elder} of the east stair
  A resident who never asks for anything
  One of the players of {instrument}
fut.asker.lc
  a child of {n}
  the oldest resident of {$home}
  a gardener from the {fut.green}
  the master of the {craft} workshop
  the watch at the {fut.gate}
  a resident who never asks for anything

fut.wish (people=18)
  for more light in {season.now}
  for the old music in the halls
  for the {festival} lamps to be lit early
  for {food} at the evening meal
  for the {herd} to be let out of the pens for a day
  for the weather to be changed for {festival}
  for a quiet day, without announcements
  for {instrument} to be played at dawn
  to be woken {time.of}
  for the {tree} by the {fut.gate} to be left alone
  for the old word for {fut.oldword}
  whether {skynight} would be clear tonight
  for the recording of their grandmother's voice
  for a set for {fut.game} in the common room
  for the doors to be painted {colour.any}, as they were
  for the smell of {fruit} in the {fut.green}, like before
  for the doors to stop greeting them by name
  for a story, any story, at bedtime
  to be told how old the {fut.wall} are
  for {drink} to be served at the watch
  for the {fut.green} to be left dark one night, for the stars
  to learn {craft} from a person, not from me
fut.wish.n
  more light in {season.now}
  the old music in the halls
  {food} at the evening meal
  a quiet day
  the {festival} lamps early
  a story at bedtime
  {drink} at the watch

fut.answer (share=0.75)
  Granted.
  Granted, within limits.
  Refused; the reason has been explained twice, once over {drink}.
  Referred to {ruler.the}.
  Granted. Nobody came, except the {herd}.
  Granted, though it is the {nth} time, and the {fut.block} have opinions.
  Considered. I will answer after the {fut.green} are watered.
  Granted, and I enjoyed it.
  Granted for one day; the day was a success, and ended with {food}.
  Granted, after the {craft} workshop was asked.
  Granted, and the {herd} were moved to make room.
  Granted, on condition of {food} for everyone.
  Referred to the keepers of {holyplace}, who said yes.
  Granted at {festival}, when the {colour.holy} lamps are lit, and not before.
  Refused. Resubmitted with {fruit}. Granted.
  Not possible. {food} offered instead, and accepted.
  Granted. {#n|resident} from the {fut.block} asked for the same.
  Answered with a riddle from {fut.game}. The resident laughed.

# what the residents were seen doing
fut.obs
  (3) {fut.res.pl} {fut.doing} in the {fut.common}.
  (2) {fut.res.pl} {fut.doing} in the {fut.common}. {fut.obscoda}
  (1) {#n|resident} {fut.doing} {fut.when.past}. {fut.obscoda}
  (1) In the {fut.common}, {fut.res.lc} {fut.doing}.

fut.res.pl (pl people=6)
  Residents
  The children
  The old ones
  The young
  The {craft} workers
  The night watch
  The families of the {fut.block}
  The players of {instrument}
  The gardeners
  The newcomers from {city2}
fut.res.lc (pl)
  residents
  the children
  the old ones
  the gardeners
  the young

fut.doing (people=14)
  kept {feast.custom}
  spent the evening at {pastime}
  planted {fruit} in the long beds
  argued about the gardens
  sang the {festival} songs
  wore {colour.mourn} for a death in the {fut.block}
  cooked {food} in the common kitchens
  brought {drink} to the watch
  repainted {motif.over} over the doors
  practised {craft} the slow way
  danced the {~dance}
  told the old stories about {mountain}
  counted {bird} from the observation deck
  walked the {herd} round the terraces
  swapped {fruit} and {veg} across the courtyard
  carried {colour.holy} lamps to {holyplace}
  sat in silence for the dead of {city}
  built a model of {focusword} out of {material}
fut.obscoda (share=0.8)
  I kept the lights on for them.
  Nobody asked me to join. I watched.
  Logged without comment.
  It went on past midnight, and so did {instrument}.
  The noise was within limits, just, until the {herd} joined in.
  Two of them asked me to record it for the {~book}.
  It rained on the {fut.green}; they did not seem to notice.
  It was the first time in {#n|cycle} that anyone had danced the {~dance}.
  They left {food} out for me afterwards. I logged it as kindness.
  The {craft} workshop lent them the old tools for it.

# the counts of the day
fut.count
  {#n|birth} this cycle, {#n|death}; the births marked with {colour.holy} cord at the {fut.gate}.
  Population of {$home} stable. The {herd} in the pens up by {#n}.
  {#nbig} meals served at {festival}; {#n} complaints, all about the {food}.
  Water use up by a {fut.part} in {season.now}, most of it in the {fut.green}.
  {#n|resident} moved from the {fut.block} to {city2}; {#n} came the other way, with their {beast}.
  Stores of {crop} at {fut.level}; of {crop2} at {fut.level}.
  {#nbig} visitors at the {fut.green} this cycle, most of them for the {fruit}.
  {#n} weddings this cycle, all in the {fut.common}, all with {feast.custom}.
fut.part
  tenth
  quarter
  third
  fifth
fut.level
  capacity
  three quarters
  half
  the usual
  a level nobody living has seen

# outside the shield
fut.outside
  {weather.now} outside the shield. Inside: within limits, and the {herd} restless.
  {skynight} visible from the observation deck; {#n|resident} went up to see it, with {drink}.
  Outside: {weather.now}. The {tree} on the slopes have turned.
  The {bird} came back to {land} this week, {#n} days late.
  (aurora=1) The lights in the north, all night. The children were allowed up to watch from the {fut.green}.
  (comet=1) The hairy star is in the evening sky again; the {craft} workshop has painted it on a door.
  (rings=1) The ring was edge-on today, a line across the sky. The {herd} did not look up.
  (moons>0) {moon} rose full over {mountain}. The {fut.green} doors were opened for it, as the old ones did.

# the old ways kept: the herds, the crafts, the feasts
fut.pens
  The {herd} in the heritage pens are well; one is lame and has been named for it.
  {#n} young {herd} born in the pens. Named by the children, badly.
  The {craft} workshop open late; {#n} pieces finished for {festival}, mostly {colour.any}.
  {fruit} picked in the {fut.green}: more than last cycle, and sweeter.
  The {~hall} swept for {feast.custom}.
fut.rite
  (faith!=machine faith!=philosophy) Lamps lit at {holyplace} for {god}, with {fruit} on the step. Attendance: {fut.attend}.
  {feast.custom} kept at {$home}. Attendance: {fut.attend}.
  (rite=memory) The names of the dead read at {holyplace}, the {colour.mourn} cloths hung. It went on long after dark.
  The {#number} bells rung for {festival} by hand, the ropes wound with {colour.holy} cloth, as the old ones did.
fut.attend (share=0.6)
  most of them
  everyone who could walk
  fewer than last cycle
  {#nbig}
  the old ones, a few children and the {herd}
  the whole {fut.block}, and their {beast}

fut.decline
  Population of {$home} down again this period.
  {#n} districts dark. Power rerouted to the others.
  Nobody has come to the {fut.green} in {#n|cycle}.
  The transit line runs empty most of the day.
  The {fut.block} closed. Its residents moved nearer the centre.
  The {herd} released from the pens; there was nobody to keep them.
  {festival} kept by {#n|resident}. The rest were too tired.
  The {craft} workshop shut. The tools are labelled and stored.
  I have stopped heating the {fut.common}. Nobody sits there now.
)VG"
